  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far)
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far), an input waits at the gateway
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far), turn runs on the gateway
  s4: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far), idle session on the gateway
  s5: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), idle session on the gateway
  s6: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input waits at the gateway, idle session on the gateway
  s7: Home is the gateway (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is kept for the designated node, idle session on the gateway
  s8: Home is the gateway (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is kept for the designated node, old home asked to end, idle session on the gateway
  s9: Home is the gateway (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is kept for the designated node, old home did not answer, idle session on the gateway
  s10: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is handed to the designated node, idle session on the gateway
  s11: Home is the designated node (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input is handed to the designated node
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s1 --> s2: you send a message
  s2 --> s3: the gateway starts the turn itself
  s3 --> s4: the answer reaches Discord
  s4 --> s5: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s5 --> s6: you send a message
  s6 --> s7: the gateway puts the input into shared custody
  s7 --> s8: the old home is asked to end its session
  s8 --> s9: the request's deadline passes without an answer
  s9 --> s10: the owner row moves to the new home
  s10 --> s10: a node reads the owner row again
  s10 --> s11: the old home ends its idle session
